# Line-ending policy: LF is canonical, in the repo and the working tree.
#
# The repo already stores every text file as LF. Without this file, a
# checkout on a machine with core.autocrlf=true (the Git-for-Windows
# default) rewrites the working tree to CRLF. Convex then regenerates
# convex/_generated/*.ts as LF, and that working-LF-vs-expected-CRLF
# mismatch shows up as a phantom "modified" api.d.ts (identical content,
# only the line-ending expectation differs). Pinning eol=lf removes the
# dependence on each machine's core.autocrlf and stops the churn.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Known binaries — never apply line-ending conversion (belt-and-suspenders;
# `text=auto` already auto-detects, these just make intent explicit).
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.pem  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
